"", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746d4"}, {"id": "469043", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746d5"}, {"id": "0ade40", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746d6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746d7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478d"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87f1"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of given orbitals which have electron density along the axis is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>xy</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>yz</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>xz</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "129339", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746d8"}, {"id": "efb828", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746d9"}, {"id": "3615ba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746da"}, {"id": "c08e25", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746db"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746dc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f49"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471c"], "question": {"text": "For hydrogen atom, energy of an electron in first excited state is \\(-3.4 \\mathrm{eV}, \\mathrm{K} . \\mathrm{E}\\). of the same electron of hydrogen atom is \\(x \\mathrm{eV}\\). Value of \\(x\\) is ______ \\(\\times 10^{-1} \\mathrm{eV}\\). (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "c6ba04", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746dd"}, {"id": "a72b25", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746de"}, {"id": "5f0503", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746df"}, {"id": "da1d6f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52d5"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of following statement/s which is/are incorrect is ______</p><p>A)&nbsp;Line emission spectra are used to study the electronic structure</p><p>B)&nbsp;The emission spectra of atoms in the gas phase show a continuous spread of wavelength from red to violet.</p><p>C)&nbsp;An absorption spectrum is like the photographic negative of an emission spectrum</p><p>D) The element helium was discovered in the sun by spectroscopic method</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4c9e80", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e2"}, {"id": "865dde", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e3"}, {"id": "689efc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e4"}, {"id": "21a291", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["6162fb766ed13040ec84f345"], "question": {"text": "<p>A ball weighing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is moving with a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the uncertainty in its velocity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, then the uncertainty in its position is _&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Rounded off to the nearest integer)</p><p>[Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Js</mi></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4c52cb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e7"}, {"id": "f29cd1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e8"}, {"id": "4472f3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746e9"}, {"id": "67c9d9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746ea"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746eb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478d"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9268"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider the following set of quantum numbers.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">A</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">B</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">C</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">D</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>The number of correct sets of quantum numbers is</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5fbea3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746ec"}, {"id": "83e437", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746ed"}, {"id": "60e897", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746ee"}, {"id": "8dc460", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746ef"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b42"], "question": {"text": "The work function of sodium metal is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If photons of wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> are incident on the metal, the kinetics energy of the ejected electrons will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>__________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "66d1e8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f1"}, {"id": "350925", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f2"}, {"id": "697b57", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f3"}, {"id": "60591a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478d"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8eee"], "question": {"text": "A certain orbital has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The number of radial nodes in this orbital is _______. (Round off to the Nearest Integer)."}, "options": [{"id": "afd501", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f6"}, {"id": "df4275", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f7"}, {"id": "8fd373", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f8"}, {"id": "3bccf8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746f9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746fa", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["6162fb766ed13040ec84f353"], "question": {"text": "The energy of one mole of photons of radiation of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Jmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is _____ .<br />(Nearest integer)<br />(Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>626</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi>Js</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>022</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "6879b5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746fb"}, {"id": "79ecb2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746fc"}, {"id": "ac75bd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746fd"}, {"id": "7c6f55", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746fe"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d92746ff", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478d"], "concepts": ["6117bbff67dbe2603c3ec24d"], "question": {"text": "A hypothetical electromagnetic wave is show below.\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fr4PCdkPiV2bLibwC2FVSi-4LDUaoYDxCrgjDSBLXdFo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />The frequency of the wave is \\(x \\times 10^{19} \\mathrm{~Hz}\\).\n\\(x =\\) ______ (nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "5e1701", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274700"}, {"id": "69c224", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274701"}, {"id": "005cc4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274702"}, {"id": "266952", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274703"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274704", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478d"], "concepts": ["6162fb796ed13040ec84f523"], "question": {"text": "The number of correct statements from the following is ...........<br />A. For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;orbital, the probability density is maximum at the nucleus<br />B. For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;orbital, the probability density first increases to maximum and then decreases sharply to zero.<br />C. Boundary surface diagrams of the orbitals encloses a region of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;probability of finding the electron.<br />D.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>-orbitals have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;angular nodes respectively<br />E. probability density of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>-orbital is zero at the nucleus<br />&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "c528a8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274705"}, {"id": "9647ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274706"}, {"id": "a357ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274707"}, {"id": "8cb194", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274708"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274709", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["6162fb766ed13040ec84f345"], "question": {"text": "<p>If the uncertainty in velocity and position of a minute particle in space are, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>26</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfenced></math> respectively. The mass of the particle in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/Ma