 finder of power <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mW</mi></math> and wavelength of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;second is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>13</mn></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (Nearest integer) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi>Js</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>:"}, "options": [{"id": "c627cf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274714"}, {"id": "775dae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274715"}, {"id": "6a5535", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274716"}, {"id": "bcbed4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274717"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274718", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5671"], "question": {"text": "The de-Broglie's wavelength of an electron in the \\(4^{\\text {th }}\\) orbit is \\(\\qquad\\) \\(\\pi \\mathrm{a}_0 \\cdot\\left(\\mathrm{a}_0=\\right.\\) Bohr's radius \\()\\)"}, "options": [{"id": "27b135", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f5f2ee0e063d9274719"}, {"id": "7a98a4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "